# Docker options for Levion's lahaina-qgki defconfig, limited to those that keep the phone's vendor modules loading.
# 2026-10-31: measured on the OnePlus 9 Pro (EvolutionX 17, running 5.4.302-levion-op9+, 48 vendor_dlkm modules,
# 4669 imported symbols): thin/modcheck.py on each variant's exported-symbol CRCs, Levion aox-ksun 7eee06f.
#
#   variant                                          modules' CRC mismatches
#   Levion unchanged                                 0
#   + PID_NS + XT_MATCH_ADDRTYPE (this file)         0
#   + CGROUP_PIDS + CGROUP_DEVICE                    880   (each new cgroup controller grows CGROUP_SUBSYS_COUNT)
#   + POSIX_MQUEUE                                   about 1040 more
#   + BRIDGE_NETFILTER  (with all of the above)      1923 in total
#
# Any mismatch (module_layout is always one) makes every vendor module refuse to load, so the phone would boot
# without Wi-Fi, audio, display. The options below it are left out on purpose; getting them needs the vendor
# modules rebuilt and vendor_dlkm flashed too (Levion's own compile.sh does that), a different and larger job.
#
# Already on in Levion: SYSVIPC, IPC_NS, UTS_NS, NET_NS, USER_NS, BRIDGE, VETH, OVERLAY_FS, IP6_NF_NAT,
# IP6_NF_TARGET_MASQUERADE, CGROUP_BPF. Also not here: IP_VS / XT_MATCH_IPVS (changes struct net; swarm only).
CONFIG_PID_NS=y
CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_MATCH_ADDRTYPE=y
